Steps to create a Python virtual environment in Windows:

1. Open Command Prompt or PowerShell.
2. Navigate to your project directory: cd path\to\your\project
3. Create the virtual environment: python -m venv myenv
4. Activate the environment: myenv\Scripts\activate
5. Install packages if needed: pip install package_name
6. Deactivate when done: deactivate



